From ea12e73afdcb40e85a7d2a7763e5ba60cface9b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:17:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/37] arm64: dts: apple: t6020-j414s: add a test variant
 without external DCPs

Both external display coprocessors are started at boot and, because the
DCP driver marks itself a wakeup path, kept powered through suspend, with
nothing connected. This board tree leaves them out, to measure what that
costs: it drops the dcpext aliases so m1n1 neither enables them nor carves
out their memory, disables the two DCPs with their DARTs and mailboxes, and
keeps only the internal DART in the display subsystem's iommus, since an
entry for a disabled DART fails the node's IOMMU setup. HDMI and USB-C
display output do not work with it.

Like t6020-j414s-pmp.dts it has the board's compatible and is left out of
the Makefile. The test compares the merged sources of both trees and allows
only those changes.

